  {
    "episode_id": 77650,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77650.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Some of the speakers, for me, got a bit too political, a bit too out of context of the memorial service, and it became too much of a political service in many ways. But the member of the clergy, his name was Nathan Baxter in his sermon, brought it back. It was a very powerful sermon, and I remember in that he said, as we act, let us not become the evil that we deplore. And I wrote that down on the program that I had, and that for me was the final result.",
