    "turn_text": "Well, it became very interesting to say the least. Lots of death threats. You cannot imagine the kind of harassment, death threats, phone calls, emails. It was a mess. And to their credit, the Capitol Police were very efficient and helpful. I had security for several months, 24-hour security because of the threats which were real. And it really did make it very difficult for my mother and family and friends because they were quite naturally were worried on the other side of that. I heard from Bishop Tutu, and I'll never forget Coretta Scott King at an event, just two weeks later. She came up to me, and she hugged me, and she talked with me for about ten minutes, and she told me that that was the right vote. She knew that Martin would be very proud of me.",
